      {
        "id": "lem-qft-lattice-ward-identities",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Exact regulated gauge and infinitesimal Ward identities",
        "reference": "research/extended-frameworks-2026-10-03/quantum-field-theory/workers/qed/proofs.md#Q6; reserved proposed inventory, exact conditional statement authored in items/lem-qft-lattice-ward-identities.md",
        "design_state": "reserved claim; complete conditional argument authored; Step-1 readiness escalated pending batch-37 carrier",
        "dependency_level": 6,
        "deps": [
          "def-qft-compact-lattice-gauge-data",
          "lem-qft-lattice-gauss-projection",
          "lem-qft-lattice-physical-evolution",
          "def-axiom-of-choice"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-qft-compact-lattice-gauge-data": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-lattice-gauss-projection": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-lattice-physical-evolution": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-axiom-of-choice": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "Assume the finite-graph model of [[def-qft-compact-lattice-gauge-data]] and the Axiom of Choice. Let $\\psi\\in\\mathcal H_{\\rm phys}$ be a normalized vector. A bounded operator $O$ has gauge charge $q=(q_x)_{x\\in V}\\in\\mathbb Z^V$ when\n$$U(\\alpha)OU(\\alpha)^\\dagger=e^{i\\sum_x q_x\\alpha_x}O.$$\nThen $\\langle\\psi,O\\psi\\rangle=0$ whenever $q\\ne0$, and any finite product of bounded gauge-charge eigenoperators has zero expectation when the sum of its charge vectors is nonzero.\n\nFor each $x$, if $O$ maps $D(G_x)$ into itself and $[G_x,O]$ extends to a bounded operator, then\n$$\\langle\\psi,[G_x,O]\\psi\\rangle=0.$$\nThe same assertions apply to $O(t)=\\mathcal U(t)^\\dagger O\\mathcal U(t)$: the finite-regulator time evolution preserves the gauge charge and the domains $D(G_x)$. These are exact operator identities for the stated regulator; no trace or path-integral identity and no continuum Ward–Takahashi statement is asserted.\n\n",
        "strategy": "direct",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "John B. Kogut, An Introduction to Lattice Gauge Theory and Spin Systems, Reviews of Modern Physics 51 (1979), §VI.C, printed pp. 694–696",
